.TH ICHNOS 1 "2026-10-21" "ichnos 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ichnos \- view, edit and remove photo metadata, safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ichnos
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B ichnos show
.RB [ \-a ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.IR FILE ...
.br
.B ichnos strip
.RB [ \-p
.IR PRESET ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR SUFFIX ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.IR FILE ...
.br
.B ichnos presets
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ichnos
shows the metadata stored in photos (EXIF, GPS, XMP, IPTC, maker notes, PNG
text) and writes cleaned copies with the tags you choose removed. Original
files are never modified and existing files are never overwritten. Each copy
is read back after writing to check that every requested change was made.
.PP
Without a command,
.B ichnos
opens the graphical application with the given files or folders.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B show
List the metadata in each file. Tags that reveal location, personal details or
device identifiers are marked.
.B \-a
also lists file-system details and values exiftool calculates.
.TP
.B strip
Write a cleaned copy of each file, named
.IR name _clean. ext
next to the original.
.TP
.B presets
Describe the presets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " PRESET" "\fR, \fP\-\-preset " PRESET
.B location
removes GPS and place names.
.B share\-safe
(the default) also removes personal details, serial numbers, thumbnails, maker
notes and edit history.
.B strip\-all
removes all metadata except what the image needs to display correctly.
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR" "\fR, \fP\-\-output\-dir " DIR
Write copies into
.I DIR
instead of next to the originals.
.TP
.BI \-s " SUFFIX" "\fR, \fP\-\-suffix " SUFFIX
Text added to copy names (default:
.BR _clean ).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be removed without writing anything.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Look inside subfolders.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every file was handled, 1 if a file could not be read or written or a copy
could not be fully cleaned, 2 if exiftool is missing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ICHNOS_EXIFTOOL
Full path of the exiftool program to use.
.TP
.B ICHNOS_THEME_DIR
Folder to read theme colours from, instead of the active Omarchy theme.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ichnos strip \-\-preset location ~/Pictures/trip/*.jpg
Remove location from a set of photos.
.TP
.B ichnos strip \-n holiday.jpg
See what share\-safe would remove from one photo.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR exiftool (1)
.SH AUTHOR
p@nos <padou.dev@proton.me>
